{"id":48,"course_id":16,"title":"RED, USE, and Kubernetes Golden Signals","summary":"Separate user symptoms from infrastructure causes.","sequence":1,"body_simplified":"## Measurement model\nGood observability starts with the question: what pain does the user feel? RED metrics cover request Rate, Error rate, and Duration. USE covers Utilization, Saturation, and Errors for resources.\n- Use RED for APIs and request-driven services.\n- Use USE for nodes, disks, queues, network interfaces, and database pools.\n- Kubernetes adds desired vs available replicas, pending Pods, restarts, unschedulable reasons, and HPA behavior.\n- Page on user impact or imminent capacity exhaustion, not every component twitch.\n\n## Inspection commands\n$ kubectl top nodes\n$ kubectl top pods -A\n$ kubectl get deploy -A\n$ kubectl get events -A --sort-by=.lastTimestamp\nLook for saturation, rollout availability, crash patterns, scheduling pressure, and whether the symptom is service-level or component-level.\n\n## Dashboard rule\nOne dashboard should answer: are users hurt, where is the blast radius, what changed, and which dependency is saturated?","body_traditional":"## Measurement model\nGood observability starts with the question: what pain does the user feel? RED metrics cover request Rate, Error rate, and Duration. USE covers Utilization, Saturation, and Errors for resources.\n- Use RED for APIs and request-driven services.\n- Use USE for nodes, disks, queues, network interfaces, and database pools.\n- Kubernetes adds desired vs available replicas, pending Pods, restarts, unschedulable reasons, and HPA behavior.\n- Page on user impact or imminent capacity exhaustion, not every component twitch.\n\n## Inspection commands\n$ kubectl top nodes\n$ kubectl top pods -A\n$ kubectl get deploy -A\n$ kubectl get events -A --sort-by=.lastTimestamp\nLook for saturation, rollout availability, crash patterns, scheduling pressure, and whether the symptom is service-level or component-level.\n\n## Dashboard rule\nOne dashboard should answer: are users hurt, where is the blast radius, what changed, and which dependency is saturated?","pinyin":"Scenario: Latency increased after a deployment.\nChecklist:\n- Check request p95/p99 and error rate by route or service.\n- Compare deployment time with rollout, restart, and HPA events.\n- Check CPU throttling, memory pressure, database pool saturation, and queue depth.\n- Move from symptom dashboard to workload and dependency dashboards.\nCommands:\n$ kubectl rollout history deploy/checkout -n payments\n$ kubectl get hpa,pods -n payments","audio_url":null,"video_url":null,"course_slug":"platform-sre-observability-kubernetes","course_category":"SRE","course_era":"Platform Academy","vocabulary":[{"id":211,"simplified":"RED metrics","traditional":"RED metrics","pinyin":"Service signals","definition":"Rate, Errors, and Duration for request-oriented services."},{"id":212,"simplified":"USE metrics","traditional":"USE metrics","pinyin":"Resource signals","definition":"Utilization, Saturation, and Errors for infrastructure resources."},{"id":213,"simplified":"Golden signals","traditional":"Golden signals","pinyin":"Reliability","definition":"Latency, traffic, errors, and saturation."},{"id":214,"simplified":"Saturation","traditional":"Saturation","pinyin":"Capacity","definition":"A signal that a resource has more demand than it can serve promptly."},{"id":215,"simplified":"Blast radius","traditional":"Blast radius","pinyin":"Impact","definition":"The scope of users, services, regions, or clusters affected by a problem."}],"flashcards":[{"id":127,"lesson_id":48,"prompt":"When should a container restart page someone?","answer":"When it correlates with user impact or high-risk service failure, not as standalone noise.","pinyin":"platform","difficulty":"beginner"},{"id":128,"lesson_id":48,"prompt":"What does RED measure?","answer":"Request rate, error rate, and duration.","pinyin":"platform","difficulty":"beginner"},{"id":129,"lesson_id":48,"prompt":"What does USE measure?","answer":"Utilization, saturation, and errors for resources.","pinyin":"platform","difficulty":"beginner"}]}
